M52XQ: gprs: on LTE, packet service registered counts as attached

connman deactivates the default bearer while Wi-Fi is in use. ofono then dropped Attached on LTE (no active context), the
cellular service disappeared and Connect failed.

--- a/src/gprs.c
+++ b/src/gprs.c
@@ -1625,7 +1625,17 @@
 		 * expect the gprs status to be unknown. That must not
 		 * result in detaching...
 		 */
-		attached = have_active_contexts(gprs);
+		/*
+		 * M52XQ: that is not enough: connman deactivates the default
+		 * bearer while Wi-Fi is in use, Attached went false, the
+		 * cellular service vanished and could not be connected again
+		 * ("not attached"). Packet service registered = attached.
+		 */
+		attached = have_active_contexts(gprs) || L_IN_SET(status,
+			NETWORK_REGISTRATION_STATUS_REGISTERED,
+			NETWORK_REGISTRATION_STATUS_REGISTERED_SMS_EUTRAN,
+			NETWORK_REGISTRATION_STATUS_ROAMING,
+			NETWORK_REGISTRATION_STATUS_ROAMING_SMS_EUTRAN);
 	else
 		attached = gprs->driver_attached && L_IN_SET(status,
 			NETWORK_REGISTRATION_STATUS_REGISTERED,
